# Files in this list belong to the GitHub repo, not the vault. ShardMind
# leaves them out of `shardmind install`, so an installed vault carries only
# what an Obsidian user needs. The repo keeps them for contributors.
#
# Gitignore semantics, negation included. See ShardMind docs/SHARD-LAYOUT.md
# §File disposition for the three-tier model.

# Contributor rules. The vault's CLAUDE.md points here for shard development.
CONTRIBUTING.md

# The shard's design contract. Describes the repo, not a vault's content.
SPEC.md

# The build order and the loop that takes it. Both are about developing the
# shard; a vault has no roadmap and no tracker.
ROADMAP.md
.claude/skills/take-next/

# Tests that import repo-only code. bootstrap-hook.test.ts imports
# .shardmind/hooks/bootstrap.ts, which the engine never installs (Tier 1), so
# in a vault the whole file would fail to load. obsidian-mind lists it the
# same way.
.claude/scripts/tests/bootstrap-hook.test.ts

# Reads .shardmind/shard.yaml and .github/workflows/ci.yml, which never
# install (Tier 1): in a vault the file would fail on its first read.
.claude/scripts/tests/shard-manifest.test.ts

# Development dependencies (the CI typecheck install). A vault never gets
# them, and on POSIX their .bin entries are symbolic links, which the engine
# rejects anywhere in a shard (WALK_SYMLINK_REJECTED).
node_modules/
